<title>UK: Screen shares set AIM debut premium.</title>
<headline>Screen shares set AIM debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in security products company Screen Plc set a 33 percent premium on their first day on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Monday.</p>
<p>By 1500 GMT the shares, issued at 3p, were quoted at 4p, although no trade was registered in the stock.</p>
<p>The placing, sponsored by Smith and Williamson with broker Ellis &amp; Partners, raised 1.8 million stg before expenses, valuing Screen at 6.0 million stg.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
